Subject: [REVIEW 03/16] Shared Thunderbolt host transport and lifecycle

Separate shared NHI/ring handling from PCI transport, extend host callbacks, and carry the shared teardown changes. This patch also carries the Qualcomm platform driver registration in pci.c (declared in nhi.h), guarded by CONFIG_USB4_QCOM. Review effects on existing PCI controllers, DMA ownership and interrupt synchronization. Since 1.122 the series no longer changes tb.c, tb.h or usb4.c here: the DP resource retry hook and the bring-up diagnostics in them are removed. Patch 12 changes tb.c for a separate resume problem.

Dependencies: Base prerequisites for the shared transport. Required by patch 05. The CONFIG_USB4_QCOM-guarded registration references qcom_usb4_host_driver and qcom_usb4_dp_driver, defined in patch 05, so the tested configuration needs 05 to link.

Source attribution: Local Surface integration; original decomposition in provenance/usb4/10-thunderbolt-share-nhi-teardown.patch through 19-thunderbolt-document-shared-ring-interrupt-ownership.patch; later changes recorded in provenance/derivation.json.

This is a review grouping of preserved source, not a new authorship claim or
an independently build-validated upstream commit. Original attribution remains
in the referenced provenance files. No new Signed-off-by trailers are added.

